  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A person whose mass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> travels from Earth to Mars in a spaceship. Neglect all other objects in sky and take acceleration due to gravity on the<br />surface of the Earth and Mars as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, respectively. Identify from the below figures, the curve that fits best for the weight of the passenger as a function of time.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/41fc8ea9-80c5-4a50-994b-108c18aa61c5-image.png\" style=\"width: 340px; height: 221px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
